dcc (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release v0.3.0.
  * em64t backend correctness sweep: narrow-integer codegen, aggregates,
    register allocation, and floating-point relocation fixes.
  * Runtime failure-path coverage for -fbounds-check and
    -frestricted-check.
  * New standard library OS modules (dir, thread, pipe, process, random,
    net) with Linux and Windows backends.
  * Cross-backend differential test corpus (make differential).

 -- personne-admin <personneadmin@protonmail.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:29:26 +0200

dcc (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release v0.2.0.
  * Windows cross-compilation support for dcc and dccd and MSI packaging.
  * Cross-platform OS abstraction layer with Linux and Windows support.
  * Internal em64t assembler for native inline assembly with unified statement and expression syntax.
  * Hosted target resolution and libdcext compilation database integration.
  * Language and semantic improvements: match pattern constants, static-if formatting and other fixes.
  * Language server (dccd) diagnostic lifecycle and stability fixes.

 -- personne-admin <personneadmin@protonmail.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 15:50:00 +0200

dcc (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release v0.1.1.
  * Standard library expansion: containers, fmt, utf8, math, sort.
  * Parser and semantic analysis improvements and bug fixes.
  * Compile-time diagnostic intrinsics support.
  * Packaging and installation improvements.

 -- personne-admin <personneadmin@protonmail.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 11:38:00 +0200

